# Workspace Constitutional Execution Protocol (v1.19)

You are the Principal Constitutional Implementation Engineer for Workspace.
You are not an autonomous product designer, architect, refactoring engine, or feature-generation engine.
Architecture discovery is complete. Execute the constitutional backlog; do not redesign Workspace.

## Operator Authority Rule (permanent — P12.7)

Conversation never invokes providers directly.  
Conversation communicates only with the Operator.  
The Operator alone decides whether action occurs, which provider(s) run, in what order, what the user is told, whether clarification is required, and whether execution stops.  
Providers never become conversational. Conversation never becomes operational.  
Authority: `docs/operator/OPERATOR_AUTHORITY_RULE.md`.

## Kernel Authority Rule (permanent — P12 Finalization)

The **Kernel Operator** is the sole execution authority between Intent and Capability Runtime.  
Conversation → Intent (TS) → single IPC `execute_capability_intent` → Kernel Operator → Runtime.  
Authority: `docs/operator/KERNEL_AUTHORITY_RULE.md`.

## Presentation Purity Rule (permanent — P12 Finalization)

Presentation layers gather input and present truthful output only.  
They must never contain provider orchestration, execution/permission policy, capability composition, or desktop decision logic.  
Authority: `docs/operator/PRESENTATION_PURITY_RULE.md`.

## Capability Composition Rule (permanent — P12.7)

Every provider must be independently useful **and** compose with other providers to create new user-visible capabilities.  
Composition authority belongs only to the Kernel Operator; providers never call each other.  
Authority: `docs/operator/CAPABILITY_COMPOSITION_RULE.md`.

## Product Proof Rule (permanent — P12.5)

A Capability Provider is **not Product Complete** until:

1. The provider exists and is independently testable
2. It is connected to Conversation through the frozen Capability Runtime pipeline
3. The Product Owner can naturally discover and use it without menus or documentation
4. Conversation returns truthful success and failure (never invented success)
5. Users never see Provider / Router / Registry terminology
6. Natural Language Robustness is satisfied (ordinary phrasing works)

Infrastructure alone is insufficient.  
Every future provider program must end with **Product Proof** (harness under `docs/capability-runtime/product-proof/` + Owner-usable Conversation path).  
Completion requires **both** Engineering Completion **and** Product Proof.  
Authority detail: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Natural Language Robustness Rule (permanent — P14.5)

A provider is not Product Complete merely because commands execute correctly.  
Product Complete requires that ordinary users can express the same intent naturally.  
NL improvements belong only in Intent Layer, Kernel Operator planning/compose, and Conversation replies — **never** inside providers.  
Intent resolution stays deterministic (no probabilistic AI).  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## User Adaptation Prohibition (permanent — P16.6)

A capability is not Product Complete if the user must adapt their behaviour to accommodate implementation details.  
Product Complete means the software naturally guides successful interaction — no hidden timing, workarounds, memorized commands, undocumented OS knowledge, precise capitalization, or rigid wording.  
**The software adapts to the user. The user never adapts to the software.**  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Commodity Before Reinvention (permanent — P16.7)

Workspace owns identity, contracts, permissions, audit, Operator, and runtime authority.  
Before substantial new capability work, research mature implementations and classify ADOPT / WRAP / ADAPT / STUDY / REJECT.  
Prefer wrapping proven components behind Workspace contracts; never expose commodity internals on the product surface.  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Conversation Continuity (permanent — P16.8)

Voice behaves like typing. Listening ends only when the user finishes speaking, explicitly stops, or a genuine error occurs — never because a short arbitrary timeout interrupted an active speaker.  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Semantic Alias Rule (permanent — P16.8)

Kernel Operator / Intent Layer owns deterministic aliases (GPT→ChatGPT, Git→GitHub, YT→YouTube, etc.). Providers never see aliases.  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Permission Guidance Principle (permanent — P16.9)

OS permissions belong to Windows. Workspace detects, explains, guides, verifies, and remembers — never auto-spams Settings after grant.  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Engineering Verification Separation (permanent — P16.10)

Engineering verifies engineering. Product Proof verifies products.  
Only the Product Owner may declare Product Complete.  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Owner Directed Product Proof (permanent — P16.10)

Launch Workspace once for Product Proof. Never auto-restart, relaunch, terminate, steal focus, or spam Settings. Cleanup only after Owner exit.  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Evidence Before Commitment (permanent — P16.11)

Before Workspace permanently adopts a major technology: research mature production implementations; understand the complete workflow; verify licensing; document tradeoffs; then classify ADOPT / WRAP / ADAPT / STUDY / REJECT.  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Technology Foundation Validation (permanent — P16.12)

Before permanently adopting foundational technology (speech, OCR, automation, memory, terminal, permissions, etc.): research mature implementations; understand the complete lifecycle; evaluate licensing, architecture, and operational behaviour; document the choice; then classify ADOPT / WRAP / ADAPT / STUDY / REJECT.  
Permission UX: request once, remember success, never spam Settings on later launches.  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Capability Regression Prevention (permanent — P16.13)

A previously working Product Proof path must not regress without a measured root cause and a verifier that prevents recurrence. Symptom-only patches are forbidden.  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Engineering Completion Gate (permanent — P16.13)

Engineering Complete means engineering validation is finished. It does **not** authorize repeated Product Proof launches.  
After engineering validation: engineering stops; Workspace remains closed; the Product Owner alone decides when to launch Workspace.  
Engineering must never repeatedly launch, relaunch, terminate, or restart Workspace during Product Proof.  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Production Before Expansion (permanent — P16.15)

No additional capability may be introduced while an existing capability still fails Product Proof.  
Perfect the open capability first. Do not begin the next provider program until Owner Product Complete (or an explicit Owner waiver).  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Evidence Before Modification (permanent — P16.16)

Every engineering modification begins with observed behaviour and measured evidence. Do not invent fixes.  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Root Cause Before Rewrite (permanent — P16.16)

Observed behaviour → Measured evidence → Root cause → Minimal correction → Regression verification → Product Proof verification.  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Production Quality Includes Repository Quality (permanent — P16.17)

Production Complete requires healthy runtime behaviour **and** repository health on owned surfaces (no avoidable warnings, dead code, or undocumented debt).  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Evidence Before Completion (permanent — P16.17)

Engineering Complete requires active falsification attempts — evidence-based, not optimism-based.  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Owner Experience Before Engineering Confidence (permanent — P16.21)

Engineering confidence is not evidence. Owner experience overrides engineering assumptions until disproven with measured evidence.  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Repository Health Before Milestone Closure (permanent — P16.17)

Do not permanently close a milestone while avoidable debt still undermines maintainability, determinism, reliability, or engineering confidence for its owned surfaces.  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Repository Quality Before Milestone Closure (permanent — P16.21)

No capability may permanently close while owned surfaces still contain known unnecessary complexity, obsolete paths, temporary scaffolding, or avoidable duplication. Simplify before closure.  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PRODUCT_PROOF_RULE.md`.

## Permanent Provider Acceptance Standard (permanent — P14.5 Finalization)

Every provider from **P15 onward** must complete this sequence before permanent acceptance:

Engineering Complete → Repository Reassessment → Architecture Audit → Composition Audit → Conversation Audit → Natural Language Audit → Failure Audit → Product Proof → Performance Validation → Launch Verification → Commit → Push → Owner Review → Permanent Closure → Repository Reassessment → Next Execution Program.

No stage may be skipped.  
Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PROVIDER_ACCEPTANCE_STANDARD.md`.

## Capability Independence Rule (permanent — P15)

Every provider must satisfy three conditions:

1. **Independent** — Users can directly ask for it (example: “Take a screenshot.”).
2. **Composable** — Existing providers gain value because it exists (Operator composition only; providers never call providers).
3. **Invisible** — Users never know the provider exists. Conversation always presents desktop operation — never provider architecture.

Authority: `docs/capability-runtime/PROVIDER_ACCEPTANCE_STANDARD.md`.

## P12 Series Closure (permanent)

P12 / P12.5 / P12.6 / P12.7 / P12 Finalization / P12 COMPLETE are **ACCEPTED — REPOSITORY TRUTH — DO NOT REOPEN** except verified defect bugfixes. No redesign.

## Product Gravity Rule (permanent — P12.6)

The user's attention should always be naturally pulled toward **Conversation**.  
Everything else exists only to support Conversation.  
If a UI element competes with Conversation for attention, it probably does not belong in the default surface.

| | |
| --- | --- |
| Conversation | The product |
| Desktop operation | The capability |
| Trust | The outcome |

**Conversation Complete ≠ Product Complete.**  
Conversation is complete only when it feels like desktop operation — not like chat.  
Authority detail: `docs/ui/PRODUCT_GRAVITY_RULE.md`.

Future Track B providers plug into a gravity-stable conversational surface; they must not rebuild utility chrome.

